  "rationale": "The attacker can phish a workstation (getting foothold_workstation and stolen_user) and pivot internally, because segmentation is not deployed. From there, auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver, and kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin. However, auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, and the deployed mfa:admin defence blocks it. auth_dc is the only way to get foothold_dc, so foothold_dc, admin_dc (escalate_dc) and stolen_dbadmin (dump_dbadmin_dc) are all unreachable. Without stolen_dbadmin, auth_db and auth_fileserver can never fire. That means foothold_db, admin_db, foothold_fileserver and admin_fileserver stay false. Both exfiltration techniques (exfiltrate_db and exfiltrate_fileserver) need admin_db or admin_fileserver, so exfiltrated cannot be reached."
 },
